# AWS Application Load Balancer with EC2 and Nginx

## 📌 Project Overview

This project demonstrates how to deploy a web server on an Amazon EC2 instance and make it accessible through an internet-facing Application Load Balancer (ALB).

The solution uses AWS EC2, a target group, security groups, and an HTTP listener to distribute incoming web traffic to an Nginx web server.

## 🎯 Objectives

- Launch an EC2 instance running Ubuntu.
- Install and run Nginx as the web server.
- Configure security groups to allow HTTP traffic on port 80.
- Create an EC2 target group and register the instance.
- Configure an internet-facing Application Load Balancer.
- Verify website accessibility through the ALB DNS endpoint.

