### Traffic Flow

1. A user sends an HTTP request to the ALB DNS address.
2. The Application Load Balancer receives traffic on port 80.
3. The ALB forwards the request to the registered EC2 target.
4. Nginx serves the website content.
5. The ALB returns the HTTP response to the user.

